15461:/private/tmp/grocer-luna-audit-8280c6e/data/92/inclusions.json:2:  {"name": "Kitchen housewares department (customer). At store 92 'Kitchen' labels a shelf department — Appliances, Coffee Appliances/Blenders, Cookware/Food Processing/Mixers, Cookware Sets/Stockpots, Bake Ware/Dinnerware/Cutting Boards, Tabletop/Plasticware/Textiles/Pantryware plus the Kitchen Gadgets/Cutlery/Cutting Boards wall run — not a service counter. The derived auto:SEAFOOD disk (pt (1127,399), r=130, bridge 20) reaches back to x=997 and closed the 14-18 pt gaps between those shelf rows; the resulting pocket held the KITCHEN label, so the SERVICE_DEPTS substring cull condemned all 2206 cells as staff. Same false positive as 658/660's 'Kitchen Gadgets' aisle. East edge 1176 = the drawn shelf outline at x=1175; the 5 pt sliver between it and the wall at x=1182 stays sealed, as does the 6 pt crevice at y 374-378 between the department's south shelf row and the seafood counter (bottom edge stops at y=374 so that crevice cannot come back as an island).",
